This target has desktop GL linked in, at the GLSL version oops-gl implements

Three arms in `libultraship`'s GL backends assume something this platform answers
differently. Two are narrowed on `__PROSPERO__`, so every other platform keeps
exactly what upstream gave it; the third is a version number.

Ship of Harkinian carries the same two narrowings against its own
`libultraship` revision - see `../ship-of-harkinian/patches/0001` and `0002`,
where the reasoning is written out in full. In short:

**`glewInit()` - nothing to load.** `gfx_opengl.cpp` calls GLEW everywhere but
Linux, because elsewhere the GL entry points past 1.1 have to be fetched from a
driver at run time. Here they do not exist to be fetched: `oops-gl` *is* the GL,
linked into the payload, every name an ordinary symbol the linker resolved.

**`SDL2/SDL_opengles2.h` - the wrong GL.** `gfx_sdl2.cpp`'s `#else` arm is
written for a Linux desktop, where SDL's GLES2 header is present. This target has
desktop GL and no GLES at all, so that include fails at `GLES2/gl2platform.h`
before anything else is parsed. The new arm goes *before* the `#else` rather than
inside it: the existing branch means "a Unix with SDL's GLES2 headers", which
stays true.

**`#version 130` - one version too high.** oops-gl's GLSL front end implements
1.20, and 1.30 is refused at compile. The fragment shader upstream generates for
the non-core desktop arm uses nothing 1.30 adds; the number is what is wrong
about it. `BuildVsShader` already asks for `#version 110` and is untouched.

`oops-gl` ever implementing 1.30 retires that third hunk - `gl2-probe`'s
`libultraship-dialect` arm asserts separately that 130 is still refused, and
whoever sees that arm fail should delete this hunk rather than the assertion.

Note what is deliberately *not* patched: the vertex-array pair in
`gfx_opengl.cpp` stays inside `#if defined(__APPLE__) || defined(USE_OPENGLES)`,
because this port genuinely does not call it. The vertex array objects oops-gl
needs come from ImGui's GL3 backend, which is a different library.

diff --git a/libultraship/src/fast/backends/gfx_opengl.cpp b/libultraship/src/fast/backends/gfx_opengl.cpp
--- a/libultraship/src/fast/backends/gfx_opengl.cpp
+++ b/libultraship/src/fast/backends/gfx_opengl.cpp
@@ -283,7 +283,7 @@ std::string GfxRenderingAPIOGL::BuildFsShader(const CCFeatures& cc_features) {
         { "texture", "texture" },
         { "vOutColor", "vOutColor" },
 #else
-        { "GLSL_VERSION", "#version 130" },
+        { "GLSL_VERSION", "#version 120" },
         { "attr", "varying" },
         { "opengles", false },
         { "core_opengl", false },
@@ -652,7 +652,7 @@ void GfxRenderingAPIOGL::DrawTriangles(float buf_vbo[], size_t buf_vbo_len, size
 }

 void GfxRenderingAPIOGL::Init() {
-#ifndef __linux__
+#if !defined(__linux__) && !defined(__PROSPERO__)
     glewInit();
 #endif

